{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And Joseph's ten brothers went down.</b> It should have said 'the sons of Jacob,' but we learn that they regretted selling him and set their hearts to deal with him as brothers and to redeem him with whatever money might be assessed upon them." "<b>Or one may</b> interpret that Scripture explains their good intention toward him, for they went down ten in number in order to pray on his behalf in a quorum of ten, since there is no sanctity in fewer than ten, as it is said (Leviticus 22:32): ״ונקדשתי בתוך בני ישראל״." "<b>And the Ramban</b> interpreted: 'And Joseph's ten brothers went down' — in order to fulfill the first of the dreams, for he would recount it to his ten brothers — for regarding it is said (Genesis 37:5–6): ״ויגד לאחיו ויוסיפו עוד שנוא אותו״ and to them he said ״והנה אנחנו מאלמים אלומים״. For Benjamin is not included in this, and now this dream was fulfilled when they bowed down to him. But the second dream, in which it is written ״והנה השמש והירח ואחד עשר כוכבים״, could not be fulfilled until Benjamin and also his father would come." "<b>And in the Midrash:</b> 'And Joseph's ten brothers went down' — Joseph said to them: whoever comes to buy grain, let his name, his father's name, and his city's name be written down, and in the evening bring me their slips. When the sons of Jacob came, each one entered through his own gate and they wrote their names; in the evening they brought the slips before Joseph — one read 'Reuben son of Jacob,' another read 'Simeon son of Jacob,' and so for all the gates. Immediately Joseph said: seal the storehouses and open one storehouse. And he gave their names to the overseer of the storehouse and said to him: when these men come to you, seize them and send them to me. Three days passed and they did not come. Immediately he took ten mighty men from Pharaoh's house and sent them on his behalf to search for them in the marketplace. They went and found them in the marketplace of harlots. And why in the marketplace of harlots? They said: Joseph was of beautiful form and beautiful appearance — perhaps he is in a brothel of harlots. Immediately they seized them and brought them before Joseph."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 42, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:19:50.937597274Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}